Virtual Machine Bench - IDE/ATAPI IRQ14 diagnostic record
Date: 2026-09-02
Branch: Working

SYMPTOM
VIDE-CDD detected the IDE/ATAPI CD-ROM, but initialization and an ISO DIR request
waited for minutes before timing out or returning no directory listing.

CAPTURED DEVICE STATE
- MODE SENSE(10), CDB 5A 00 2A 00 00 00 00 00 90 00 00 00
- 28-byte response prepared, task-file status 48h (DRDY + DRQ)
- Later TEST UNIT READY completed with CHECK CONDITION for pending Unit Attention
- No READ(10) sector transfer had begun during the stalled DIR capture

CAPTURED INTERRUPT STATE
- Slave PIC IRR/ISR/line: 40h / 40h / 40h (local IRQ6 = system IRQ14)
- Master PIC ISR: 04h (cascade IRQ2 in service)
- Neither controller could deliver another IRQ14 while the cascade remained in service
- CPU repeatedly executed VIDE-CDD's timeout loop at 0255:12D9-135Dh

DRIVER FORENSICS
VIDE-CDD 2.14 SHA-256:
1D74D7CA6CDF790D86136C06EE06F97ED2F3B4731EC272D07A6FE5EBCA88A9F1
The decoded wait path tests BDA byte 40:8Eh bit 7 before reading IDE status.

ROOT CAUSE
The system BIOS initialized INT 76h to the generic default_int handler, which
performed only IRET. An acknowledged IRQ14 therefore left the slave IRQ6 and
master cascade IRQ2 in service. This violated the IBM AT fixed-disk interrupt
contract expected by the DOS driver.

CORRECTION
Firmware/atbios.asm now installs int76. The handler preserves AX and DS, sets
BDA 40:8Eh bit 7, sends non-specific EOI to slave port A0h and then master port
20h, restores registers, and executes IRET.

BUILD VERIFICATION
- System BIOS assembled successfully at exactly 65,536 bytes.
- Firmware/atbios.rom and Debug-output Firmware/atbios.rom hashes match.
- VirtualComputer.Modern solution: build succeeded, 0 warnings, 0 errors.

REMAINING GUEST VERIFICATION
Cold-boot the rebuilt emulator, load VIDE-CDD and MSCDEX, list the mounted ISO,
and read files. Capture Dump All again if IRQ14 remains in service or a packet
phase fails. Do not bypass the ISA IDE task file or the cascaded PIC path.

HOST UI FOLLOW-UP
The Disc Box Optical page previously returned silently when Mount was clicked
with an empty path. The live Debug Disc-Box folder was also empty at inspection.
Mount now opens an ISO picker rooted in Disc Box when needed, validates the
selected file, and displays callback/file/mount failures instead of silently
doing nothing. This changes host media handling only; the selected ISO still
enters the guest exclusively through IdeController.MountCdRom and IDE/ATAPI.

NOT READY / UNIT ATTENTION FOLLOW-UP
The 2026-09-02 01:12:36 diagnostic dump at the DOS `Not ready reading drive D:`
prompt showed media present, no active transfer, clear PIC IRR/ISR, and sense
06/28/00. The ATAPI trace recorded one TEST UNIT READY and two READ TOC commands
all receiving the same media-change CHECK CONDITION. Root cause was
UnitAttentionPending remaining set until REQUEST SENSE; VIDE-CDD retried READ
TOC directly. The controller now consumes unit attention upon its first CHECK
CONDITION while retaining sense data for REQUEST SENSE.

DIR D: STATUS-POLL FOLLOW-UP
The 2026-09-02 10:50:58 dump showed media present, unit attention clear, no
active transfer, and both PICs idle. The CPU was looping in VIDE-CDD at
0255:12D9-1331, repeatedly reading status port 1F7h. The loop masks BSY|DSC and
waits for DSC=1 with BSY=0; the emulated completed device returned 40h (DRDY
only). Ready/reset, data-request, successful completion, and error states now
include DSC, yielding idle 50h and DRQ 58h while retaining the normal ISA IDE
task-file and IRQ14 paths.
